# The CSP in vercel.json pins a sha256 of the inline theme script in
# index.html, and a hash is over bytes: checked out with CRLF, that same script
# hashes differently, every prerendered page fails the CSP rule in
# check-site.mjs, and the build stops. Nothing is wrong with the site when that
# happens — only with the line endings in the working copy. Pinning LF keeps a
# Windows clone building the same bytes as the deployment does.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git neither converts nor diffs them. The screenshot hashes in
# public/shots/ are content hashes for the same reason as above.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
